[quote][b]Subscribing only gives you the example emblems.[/b]
To use [b]your own pictures[/b], you also need the free [b]Custom Flags app[/b]. One click to download:
[h1][url=https://github.com/idiotgamster420/stellaris-custom-flags/releases/latest/download/StellarisFlagUploader-Setup.exe]⬇ Download for Windows[/url][/h1]
[h1][url=https://github.com/idiotgamster420/stellaris-custom-flags/releases/latest/download/Stellaris_Flag_Uploader-x86_64.AppImage]⬇ Download for Linux[/url][/h1]
Then follow the 6 steps below. It takes about 5 minutes.[/quote]

[h1]Custom Flags: put your own pictures on your Stellaris flag[/h1]

Use any picture as your empire's flag, pick any colour, and design your own emblems. No modding experience needed. Free and open source.

[h2]What you need[/h2]
[list]
[*]Stellaris from Steam.
[*]A Windows 10/11 PC or a Linux PC.
[*]About 5 minutes.
[/list]

[h2]Step 1: Subscribe to this mod[/h2]
Click the green [b]Subscribe[/b] button on this page. Steam downloads it for you.

[h2]Step 2: Download the free Custom Flags app[/h2]
The app is what lets you add your own pictures. This mod alone only gives you the examples.
[list]
[*][b]Windows:[/b] [url=https://github.com/idiotgamster420/stellaris-custom-flags/releases/latest/download/StellarisFlagUploader-Setup.exe]click here to download the Windows installer[/url]
[*][b]Linux:[/b] [url=https://github.com/idiotgamster420/stellaris-custom-flags/releases/latest/download/Stellaris_Flag_Uploader-x86_64.AppImage]click here to download the AppImage[/url]
[/list]
It saves to your [b]Downloads[/b] folder. (Steam may show a "you are leaving Steam" page first. Click [b]Continue to external site[/b].)

[h2]Step 3: Install and open the app[/h2]
[b]On Windows:[/b]
[olist]
[*]Open your Downloads folder and double-click [i]StellarisFlagUploader-Setup.exe[/i].
[*]If a blue box says [b]"Windows protected your PC"[/b], don't worry. Click [b]More info[/b], then click [b]Run anyway[/b]. (Windows shows this for any program from a small creator. The app is free and its code is public on GitHub.)
[*]Click [b]Next[/b] through the installer, then [b]Finish[/b]. The app ([b]Stellaris Flag Uploader[/b]) opens by itself.
[/olist]
[b]On Linux:[/b]
[olist]
[*]Open your Downloads folder and right-click the AppImage file.
[*]Choose [b]Properties[/b], go to [b]Permissions[/b], and tick [b]Allow executing file as program[/b]. Close the window.
[*]Double-click the file. The app opens.
[/olist]
The first time the app opens, it quietly creates a second mod on your computer, named just [b]Custom Flags[/b]. Your own pictures go in there.

[h2]Step 4: Add your picture[/h2]
[olist]
[*]In the app, stay on the [b]Emblems[/b] tab and click [b]Upload Images[/b].
[*]Pick a picture from your computer (PNG or JPG works best).
[*]Your picture appears on a flag preview. That's how it will look in the game.
[*]Want the picture to cover the whole flag? Tick [b]Fill the whole flag[/b].
[/olist]
You can also make your own colours ([b]Colours[/b] tab) or design emblems and backgrounds ([b]Maker[/b] tab), but you don't have to.

[h2]Step 5: Turn on the mods in the Paradox launcher[/h2]
[olist]
[*]If the Paradox launcher (the window with the [b]Play[/b] button) is open, close it. Then start Stellaris from Steam so it opens again.
[*]On the left of the launcher, click [b]Playsets[/b] (on some versions it's [b]Mods[/b]).
[*]Click [b]Add more mods[/b].
[*]Tick [b]both[/b] of these mods, then close that list:
[list]
[*][b]Custom Flags - Your Own Flags, Emblems & Colours[/b] (this Workshop mod)
[*][b]Custom Flags[/b] (just those two words, the mod the app made)
[/list]
[*]Make sure this playset is the one selected at the top of the launcher.
[/olist]

[h2]Step 6: Use your flag in the game[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Click [b]Play[/b].
[*]Make a new empire (or edit one) and go to the [b]flag[/b] screen.
[*]In the list of emblem categories, click [b]Custom[/b]. Your picture is there. Click it.
[/olist]
Done! Your picture is now your flag.

[quote][b]Got it working?[/b] A thumbs up helps other players find it, and I'd love to see your flag. Post a screenshot in the comments![/quote]

[h2]Changing things later[/h2]
Open the app ([b]Stellaris Flag Uploader[/b] in your Start menu on Windows, or your app menu on Linux), make your changes, then [b]close and restart Stellaris[/b]. The game only looks for new flags when it starts.

[h2]Something not working?[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]I don't see "Custom" in the flag screen.[/b] Go back to Step 5. Check both mods ([b]Custom Flags - Your Own Flags, Emblems & Colours[/b] and [b]Custom Flags[/b]) are ticked and that playset is selected, then start the game again.
[*][b]I see the examples but not my picture.[/b] The mod named just [b]Custom Flags[/b] (the one the app made) isn't turned on. Do Step 5 again and tick it.
[*][b]My new picture doesn't show up.[/b] Close Stellaris completely and start it again.
[*][b]The app says "Stellaris wasn't found".[/b] Stellaris has to be installed through Steam. Start it once from Steam, then open the app again.
[*][b]My friends can't see my flag in multiplayer.[/b] The game doesn't send pictures to other players. Your friends need the same pictures in their app too.
[/list]

[h2]Good to know[/h2]
[list]
[*]Only changes how flags look. Safe for multiplayer, and it shouldn't affect achievements.
[*]Works alongside UI Overhaul Dynamic. If you use custom colours from the app with it, the two colour picker screens switch back to the normal game layout.
[*]Not affiliated with or endorsed by Paradox Interactive.
[/list]
